<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Device manifest for the Samsung Galaxy A36 5G (a36xq).

    The stock vendor image already ships one fragment per prebuilt HAL under
    /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/*.xml (all of them are in proprietary-files.txt),
    so nothing that a prebuilt service declares has to be repeated here.

    What is left is the content of the stock `manifest_parrot.xml`, which the
    stock build never merged into the vendor image.

    There is deliberately no <sepolicy> element here. assemble_vintf is invoked
    with BOARD_SEPOLICY_VERS and stamps that value into the generated manifest;
    the vendor policy in this image is built from source at the platform's
    version, so hardcoding the stock value only fails the build:

      Cannot override existing value 202404 with BOARD_SEPOLICY_VERS
      (which is 202604).

    The stock manifest_parrot.xml says 202404 because the stock vendor image is
    SDK 35 (dump/vendor/build.prop: ro.vendor.build.version.sdk=35). That
    describes the stock prebuilt policy blobs, which this tree does not use.

    target-level="202404" is kept: it describes the HAL interfaces the prebuilt
    vendor services implement, and it is what the stock vendor manifest declares.
-->
<manifest version="8.0" type="device" target-level="202404">
    <!-- vendor/samsung/hal-server/bluetooth, only declared in manifest_parrot.xml -->
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>vendor.samsung.hardware.bluetooth</name>
        <fqname>ISehBluetooth/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
